WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.240
America is the richest and
most powerful country in history.

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:06.940
But America's rise to number one
was actually quite unexpected.

00:00:07.359 --> 00:00:10.071
In fact, most of North
America was ignored for

00:00:10.072 --> 00:00:12.660
more than a hundred
years after it was discovered.

00:00:12.995 --> 00:00:16.420
Here's a map that was made right before
Christopher Columbus discovered America.

00:00:16.685 --> 00:00:19.715
The Vikings said they had
discovered an island somewhere over

00:00:19.716 --> 00:00:22.600
here, but no one realized
that it was actually a continent.

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:27.240
So Columbus believed that he could find a
trade route to Asia by sailing west.

00:00:27.745 --> 00:00:30.200
But actually he found some islands in the
Caribbean Sea.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.949
Columbus didn't find the
spices he was expecting,

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:35.321
but he still believed
that he was close to India.

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:37.877
So he called the natives
Indians, got some goodies,

00:00:37.878 --> 00:00:40.180
and took them back to
the king and queen of Spain.

00:00:40.555 --> 00:00:41.800
[Columbus] Hey, your majesties!

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:43.520
I just got back from Asia!

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:44.600
[King] Great!

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:45.880
Where are the spices?

00:00:46.465 --> 00:00:51.480
Well, uh, we haven't found the spices
yet, but they've got lots and lots of gold!

00:00:52.039 --> 00:00:53.540
Now you're talking, Columbus!

00:00:53.925 --> 00:00:57.860
Go back, tell them all to be Christians,
and bring back that gold!

00:00:58.759 --> 00:01:03.160
A few years before Columbus claimed the
West Indies for Spain, the Portuguese had

00:01:03.161 --> 00:01:06.220
discovered that they could reach Asia by
sailing around Africa.

00:01:06.774 --> 00:01:09.829
So Spain and Portugal drew a line
right down the middle of the map,

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:12.185
and they agreed that all
the non-Christian lands

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:14.555
on this side of the line
would belong to Portugal,

00:01:14.602 --> 00:01:17.165
and everything on the other
side would belong to Spain.

00:01:17.669 --> 00:01:21.366
So the Portuguese sailed to Asia
and built a huge trading empire,

00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:24.360
and the Spanish got busy
conquering their half of the world.

00:01:24.829 --> 00:01:27.418
All of the interesting parts
of the Americas were down here

00:01:27.443 --> 00:01:29.980
where there was lots of
gold, silver, and people.

00:01:30.509 --> 00:01:31.960
So that's where the Spanish went.

00:01:32.769 --> 00:01:37.474
Actually, the Spanish also sent an
expedition into North America in 1539,

00:01:37.799 --> 00:01:39.448
but they didn't find gold and silver,

00:01:39.485 --> 00:01:43.340
so they mostly ignored all these useless
lands up here in North America.

00:01:43.949 --> 00:01:46.780
The English actually sent an
explorer to North America while

00:01:46.781 --> 00:01:49.341
the Spanish were still exploring
the islands in the Caribbean.

00:01:49.599 --> 00:01:52.380
That was 16 years before the Spanish
discovered Florida.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:55.789
But after that, the English
waited almost a hundred years

00:01:55.813 --> 00:01:57.741
before they tried
to colonize America.

00:01:58.155 --> 00:02:02.280
England's first colony was established at
Roanoke, North Carolina in 1585.

00:02:02.969 --> 00:02:05.851
But the same year, England got busy
fighting a war with Spain,

00:02:05.945 --> 00:02:08.100
and that colony mysteriously disappeared.

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:11.480
So they tried again at Jamestown,
and this time it worked.

00:02:11.995 --> 00:02:14.000
Next the Pilgrims arrived in Plymouth.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:17.096
The Pilgrims were strict
Christians who outlawed

00:02:17.097 --> 00:02:19.581
bad stuff like gambling
and celebrating Christmas.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:22.630
Soon lots and lots of people
were coming to America,

00:02:22.655 --> 00:02:25.800
and before long the east coast
was covered with British colonies.

00:02:26.375 --> 00:02:28.009
Meanwhile, the French
were busy claiming

00:02:28.034 --> 00:02:30.461
all of the land in the
middle of North America.

00:02:30.575 --> 00:02:36.221
Now it's 1754, and it's time for a war to
figure out who really owns what in America.

00:02:36.269 --> 00:02:39.427
New France has a population
of about 60,000 people,

00:02:39.428 --> 00:02:41.980
so they team up with some
Indian tribes to help them fight.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:44.840
That's why it's called, "The
French and Indian War."

00:02:45.234 --> 00:02:48.103
The British colonies have a population
of more than a million people,

00:02:48.314 --> 00:02:50.360
and they also team up
with some Indian tribes.

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:51.900
Who do you think won?

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:54.800
That's right, the British beat the French.

00:02:55.344 --> 00:02:57.937
At the same time there was
also a big war back in Europe,

00:02:58.023 --> 00:03:00.823
and when it was over, it
was time to redraw the map.

00:03:01.286 --> 00:03:03.792
France gave half of
Louisiana to Spain before

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:06.040
the war was over to make
sure Britain didn't get it.

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:10.160
Then after the war, France had to give the
other half of Louisiana to Britain.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.820
France also had to give Canada to Britain.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:15.382
Now Britain had lots
of land in America,

00:03:15.407 --> 00:03:18.180
but Britain had also spent
lots of money on the war.

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:19.760
And now they needed money.

00:03:20.124 --> 00:03:23.600
[Britain] Hey colonies, you know that
expensive war we helped you win?

00:03:23.904 --> 00:03:25.180
[America] Yeah, thanks for the help.

00:03:25.614 --> 00:03:26.900
Sure, no problem.

00:03:27.059 --> 00:03:30.249
By the way, we're going
to start collecting lots and

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:32.760
lots of taxes to pay for
all the help we give you.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:33.880
What?

00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:34.910
You never help us.

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:36.870
We're the ones who are always helping you.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:39.660
And how can you tax
us if we don't get to vote?

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:44.251
The colonists weren't happy with
the new taxes, and the disagreement

00:03:44.252 --> 00:03:47.640
turned into a fight, and
from a fight into a revolution.

00:03:48.172 --> 00:03:50.685
On the 4th of July, 1776,

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:53.528
the Americans declared their
independence from Great Britain.

00:03:53.894 --> 00:03:57.360
And that was the beginning of the United
States of America, right?

00:03:57.940 --> 00:03:58.940
Not quite.

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:02.640
It would be five more years before the
Americans won their war of independence.

00:04:03.055 --> 00:04:05.780
And after they had won their freedom,
they had a new problem.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:08.760
The government they had
created was a complete mess.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:12.052
The thirteen colonies had
essentially become thirteen

00:04:12.053 --> 00:04:14.840
independent countries that
were only united in name.

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:18.240
The new nation was failing, and it was
failing fast.

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:21.849
So the founding fathers wrote
a new constitution and created

00:04:21.850 --> 00:04:24.780
an entirely new federal
government that actually worked.

00:04:25.298 --> 00:04:27.099
The new constitution became official

00:04:27.164 --> 00:04:30.308
when nine states had
ratified it, and in 1789,

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:34.260
George Washington was elected the first
president of the United States.

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:39.060
But the USA was only this big, and all
the land over here belonged to Spain.

00:04:39.505 --> 00:04:41.220
So how did America get more land?

00:04:41.565 --> 00:04:45.880
Well, over in France, a guy named Napoleon
seized power and started conquering Europe.

00:04:46.325 --> 00:04:49.661
Napoleon also wanted to build
an empire in America, so he made

00:04:49.662 --> 00:04:52.840
a deal with Spain that would
give Louisiana back to France.

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:57.440
But the Americans needed to use the
Mississippi River to send goods to and

00:04:57.441 --> 00:04:59.651
from other places, and
they were afraid of what

00:04:59.652 --> 00:05:01.600
Napoleon might do if
he controlled the river.

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:05.200
So America asked France
to sell New Orleans to them.

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:09.620
[Napoleon] You know my plans
for a great empire in North America.

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:12.340
But now I must invade Britain.

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:16.380
[Talleyrand] We can build our empire
in America after we defeat the British.

00:05:16.785 --> 00:05:21.100
But if the Americans discover our plans
for America, they will support Britain,

00:05:21.285 --> 00:05:22.300
which could be fatal.

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:28.880
But if we sell Louisiana to the Americans,
they will be our friends forever,

00:05:29.175 --> 00:05:30.900
and Britain will be ours.

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:34.388
It would be foolish to
sell our largest territory,

00:05:34.389 --> 00:05:37.421
and the Americans
only want New Orleans.

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:38.000
Enough!

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:39.560
I've made up my mind.

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:40.920
We will sell it all.

00:05:41.115 --> 00:05:43.380
The money will fund our war with Britain.

00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:47.820
And so America bought
Louisiana for 15 million dollars.

00:05:48.325 --> 00:05:51.721
America had just doubled in size,
and that was good because

00:05:51.746 --> 00:05:55.260
America's population was also
almost doubling every 20 years.

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:58.886
In those days, the average
American family had 7 children,

00:05:58.954 --> 00:06:01.221
and all those kids
needed some place to live.

00:06:01.385 --> 00:06:06.217
So lots of Americans moved west, where
there was lots and lots of unclaimed land.

00:06:06.545 --> 00:06:08.171
Does anyone own this land?

00:06:08.765 --> 00:06:09.765
Of course not.

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:12.640
Great, because now it's mine.

00:06:13.055 --> 00:06:15.415
But these lands, my hunting grounds.

00:06:15.849 --> 00:06:17.140
That's not proper English.

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:20.540
You're supposed to say, these lands
WERE my hunting grounds.

00:06:20.911 --> 00:06:21.917
Huh?

00:06:22.299 --> 00:06:25.304
In 1819, America bought Florida from Spain,

00:06:25.329 --> 00:06:27.014
and agreed that this line right here

00:06:27.039 --> 00:06:30.000
would be the border between
the United States and New Spain.

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:33.455
Just two years later, Mexico
won its independence from Spain,

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:35.401
and America had a new neighbor.

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:38.376
The northern territories of
Mexico were sparsely populated

00:06:38.401 --> 00:06:39.887
and difficult to control,

00:06:39.912 --> 00:06:43.080
so the Mexican government invited
Americans to settle in Texas.

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:46.118
These settlers quickly
outnumbered the Mexicans,

00:06:46.197 --> 00:06:48.701
and before long, the Texans
broke free from Mexico

00:06:48.782 --> 00:06:51.100
 and created their
own independent republic.

00:06:51.385 --> 00:06:52.385
Yee-haw!

00:06:54.770 --> 00:06:56.692
We want to join the USA.

00:06:57.176 --> 00:06:58.285
Do you have slaves?

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:01.480
Yes, we do, and we're proud of it.

00:07:01.842 --> 00:07:04.419
Sorry, we don't need
any more slave states.

00:07:04.893 --> 00:07:05.771
[9 years later...]

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:09.140
Hey guys, I'm president
now and this is ours.

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:12.068
In 1845, the United
States changed its mind

00:07:12.069 --> 00:07:14.360
and let the Republic
of Texas join the Union.

00:07:14.805 --> 00:07:17.560
Disputes over the border of
Texas led to a war with Mexico.

00:07:18.010 --> 00:07:21.349
At the end of the war, the United States
paid Mexico 15 million dollars,

00:07:21.412 --> 00:07:24.480
and took the northern parts of
Mexico that President Polk wanted.

00:07:24.905 --> 00:07:27.037
Just five years later, the
United States also bought

00:07:27.038 --> 00:07:30.180
another piece of land from
Mexico for 10 million dollars.

00:07:30.467 --> 00:07:31.975
Meanwhile, the British agreed

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:35.721
to let the Americans have all of
the Oregon Territory below this line,

00:07:35.817 --> 00:07:38.300
as long as the British could
have everything above the line.

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:41.144
And so, in just 50 years of great luck,

00:07:41.292 --> 00:07:43.070
and one ugly war with Mexico,

00:07:43.335 --> 00:07:45.660
America now stretched from sea to sea.

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:48.336
And now there was
nowhere left to expand...

00:07:48.449 --> 00:07:49.784
Unless...

00:07:50.766 --> 00:07:52.176
[American] Hello? Uncle Sam?

00:07:52.346 --> 00:07:54.484
I’ve found an island in
the middle of the ocean.

00:07:54.734 --> 00:07:56.319
Can I claim it for the U.S.?

00:07:56.645 --> 00:07:59.681
[Uncle Sam] Hmm. We might
need that for World War 2.

00:07:59.865 --> 00:08:01.271
Does anyone live there?

00:08:01.722 --> 00:08:02.740
No, sir.

00:08:02.843 --> 00:08:04.843
Is it covered with bird droppings?

00:08:05.124 --> 00:08:06.124
Yes, sir!

00:08:06.539 --> 00:08:10.222
Congratulations son,
you’re standing on U.S. soil.

00:08:10.776 --> 00:08:13.253
Actually, sir, I
wouldn’t call this soil.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:16.060
By the way, the Guano
Island Act is still a law.

00:08:16.061 --> 00:08:18.399
So if you're tired of paying
way too much for rent,

00:08:18.512 --> 00:08:20.468
go find yourself
an island to occupy.

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:22.540
Wow. Everything is great.

00:08:22.945 --> 00:08:26.820
Right after the Americans got California,
word spread that gold had been discovered.

00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:30.380
And lots and lots of people rushed to
California to help dig up the gold.

00:08:30.950 --> 00:08:33.980
Up in the Oregon Territory,
there was lots of free farmland.

00:08:34.385 --> 00:08:37.480
America was thriving and
there was peace on all sides.

00:08:38.099 --> 00:08:40.418
But there was a big problem on the inside

00:08:40.647 --> 00:08:42.720
and that was the problem of slavery.

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:45.869
In northern states,
slavery was illegal,

00:08:45.932 --> 00:08:49.340
and many considered it to be a
great evil that must be stopped.

00:08:50.020 --> 00:08:53.160
In the south, slavery was an
important part of the economy.

00:08:53.855 --> 00:08:56.580
The Americans had been
arguing about slavery for decades.

00:08:57.113 --> 00:08:58.539
But everything came to a head

00:08:58.688 --> 00:09:02.004
when Abraham Lincoln was
elected president in 1860.

00:09:02.495 --> 00:09:05.900
Many people in the south believed that
Lincoln would abolish slavery.

00:09:06.209 --> 00:09:08.518
So most of the slave
states separated from

00:09:08.519 --> 00:09:10.880
the United States and
made their own country.

00:09:11.289 --> 00:09:14.341
That led to a big civil war,
lots of people died,

00:09:14.623 --> 00:09:16.663
the north won,
the slaves were freed,

00:09:16.834 --> 00:09:19.080
and the United States
was united again.

00:09:19.374 --> 00:09:20.281
[2 years later...]

00:09:20.529 --> 00:09:24.200
I'm sorry to hear about the
assassination of President Lincoln.

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:26.666
Yeah, another assassin
tried to kill me on

00:09:26.667 --> 00:09:29.260
the same night, but I
survived the stabbing.

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:30.400
That's terrible.

00:09:30.780 --> 00:09:35.900
I mean, it's terrible that you were
stabbed, but I'm glad that you survived.

00:09:36.265 --> 00:09:39.440
By the way, the Tsar wants America to have
Alaska.

00:09:39.855 --> 00:09:41.320
How much can you pay for it?

00:09:41.585 --> 00:09:45.880
I think we could do 5 million,
maybe 5.5 million, but not more.

00:09:46.609 --> 00:09:48.120
How about 7 million?

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:49.760
Sure.

00:09:49.815 --> 00:09:52.480
Great, I have approval for 7 million.

00:09:52.989 --> 00:09:54.460
We can make the treaty tomorrow.

00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:56.320
Can we do it tonight?

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:58.720
I should have asked for more money.

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:02.260
Great, now America has
another huge chunk of land.

00:10:02.639 --> 00:10:04.920
Now it just needs a few tropical islands.

00:10:05.380 --> 00:10:06.520
Hey, look at that!

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:10.000
Some American businessmen have taken
control of the Hawaiian Islands,

00:10:10.180 --> 00:10:12.800
and they're asking the
United States to annex them.

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:15.680
But the President of the United States
said, "No!"

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:19.436
He believed that America must
be a just and law-abiding nation

00:10:19.491 --> 00:10:23.060
that never misuses its great power
to take advantage of the weak.

00:10:23.624 --> 00:10:27.204
But others feared that if America didn't
get involved in the affairs of Hawaii,

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:31.353
another great power like Germany or Japan
would come and take the islands,

00:10:31.385 --> 00:10:34.400
and use them as a base to
attack America in a future war.

00:10:34.935 --> 00:10:38.580
Should America mind its own business,
or should it mind its own interests?

00:10:39.345 --> 00:10:43.160
America's policy of staying out of other
nations' conflicts was about to be tested

00:10:43.161 --> 00:10:46.440
because something was brewing in Cuba,
and it wasn't coffee.

00:10:46.905 --> 00:10:49.220
Cuba was in the middle
of a war for independence.

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:52.343
Almost all of Spain's other
colonies had already won their

00:10:52.344 --> 00:10:55.340
independence from Spain after
the American and French revolutions.

00:10:55.930 --> 00:10:59.700
But Cuba, Puerto Rico, and the Philippines
were still colonies of Spain.

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:03.660
The Cuban war for independence was
constantly in American newspapers,

00:11:03.980 --> 00:11:06.820
and most Americans sympathized with the
revolutionaries.

00:11:07.280 --> 00:11:11.825
In 1898, after an American warship sank in
a mysterious explosion,

00:11:12.017 --> 00:11:15.060
the U.S. told Spain to leave Cuba or else.

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:18.440
Spain responded by declaring
war on the United States.

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:22.418
Then the U.S. quickly captured Cuba,
Puerto Rico, and the Philippines,

00:11:22.626 --> 00:11:26.129
effectively bringing an end to
what remained of the Spanish Empire

00:11:26.228 --> 00:11:28.361
that Christopher Columbus had begun.

00:11:28.420 --> 00:11:29.698
During the Spanish-American War,

00:11:29.771 --> 00:11:33.900
the U.S. also annexed Hawaii, which
was becoming an important naval base.

00:11:34.514 --> 00:11:36.507
After the war, the president was shot,

00:11:36.731 --> 00:11:41.460
and so the young and energetic Theodore
Roosevelt unexpectedly became president.

00:11:42.270 --> 00:11:44.944
Hey, Columbia, we want
to build a canal right here.

00:11:45.426 --> 00:11:48.038
Sure, just pay us 10 million dollars.

00:11:48.596 --> 00:11:49.596
It’s a deal.

00:11:51.583 --> 00:11:54.993
Actually, we changed our
mind. You can’t build a canal.

00:11:55.493 --> 00:11:57.190
What? But we made a deal.

00:11:57.578 --> 00:11:58.409
Sorry.

00:12:00.379 --> 00:12:03.280
Hey, Panama, welcome to the Club of
Countries.

00:12:03.615 --> 00:12:05.520
We want to build a canal right here.

00:12:06.225 --> 00:12:07.640
Sure, go ahead.

00:12:08.300 --> 00:12:12.048
While Roosevelt was president, he built
up the second largest navy in the world,

00:12:12.232 --> 00:12:15.680
and used this powerful navy to
influence global politics.

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:20.049
The Americans finished building
the Panama Canal in 1914,

00:12:20.233 --> 00:12:22.030
allowing the powerful U.S. Navy

00:12:22.096 --> 00:12:25.200
to quickly move between
the Atlantic and Pacific Oceans.

00:12:25.670 --> 00:12:30.120
America had become a world power,
and World War I had just begun.

00:12:31.244 --> 00:12:33.040
If you want me to make
more videos like this,

00:12:33.104 --> 00:12:34.408
please subscribe to let me know,

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:36.560
and be sure to watch
the next video right here.

00:12:37.152 --> 00:12:38.951
If you want to learn more
about American history,

00:12:38.998 --> 00:12:41.353
I'll leave notes and
clarifications in the description.

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:42.660
See you next time!

